  "body": "## What\n\n- Establish `internal/core` and Python `core` and `shell` packages, with depguard and import-linter contracts plus core-scoped Ruff `TID251`.\n- Add jscpd duplication, Go deadcode and Python vulture gates, and Go, Python, and Biome complexity thresholds to `mise run check`.\n- Record a deliberately failing task run for each gate.\n\n## Why\n\nThe operator required a pure functional core and mechanical duplicate, dead code, and complexity checks before phase 2 implementation. Issues #58, #62, and #63 share the same tool configuration files.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Worker: Codex, GPT-6. Tool versions: golangci-lint 2.14.0 with depguard v2.2.1, import-linter 2.15, Ruff 0.16.9, jscpd 5.3.2, deadcode from `golang.org/x/tools` 0.50.0, vulture 2.16, and Biome 2.5.14.\n- [Failing examples for all eight gates](https://github.com/tbhb/agent-orchestration-poc/blob/b190cc5/reports/inputs/gates-failing-examples-2026-09-26.md).\n- Local `mise run check` exited 0 after all probes were removed. `mise run build` exited 0. Commit hooks passed on each of the three commits. [CI check](https://github.com/tbhb/agent-orchestration-poc/actions/runs/36276849929/job/108501162985) and [docs build](https://github.com/tbhb/agent-orchestration-poc/actions/runs/36276849924/job/108501162840) passed.\n- Local `mise run docs:check-links` reached the build but Chromium failed to launch in this sandbox. The validator then reported three `/workflow/` links, including two in untouched pages. The CI docs job passed on Linux.\n\n## Docs\n\nUpdated worker instructions, both language rules, three conventions pages, the tooling inventory, and decision records 0003 and 0004. The existing Vale exemptions for the Go rules and Go conventions remain because a temporary lint run found 87 inherited alerts across the two pages. The new sections were checked for alerts.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Green CI\n- [x] Docs updated\n- [x] No secrets in committed evidence\n- [x] Evidence committed\n\nRefs: #58\nRefs: #62\nRefs: #63\n",
